 A simple Windows Forms frontend is in `src/SnowPakTool.Desktop`. Its first tab handles PAK unpacking, workspace merging, and repacking. The **Experience / Ranks** tab displays and edits the `rankExp` progression values in `[ps]/rank_settings.sso`, shows the 17-season maximum of 1,163,997 XP, provides a collapsible region XP checklist with a selected subtotal, and totals the current rank progression values needed to reach level 30. The updated XP progression uses an exponential curve, with a steepness slider beside the curve preview and an XP reduction slider below it; the reduction amount appears beneath that slider. Opening the tab, restoring control settings, or adjusting the preview does not stage any file changes. Save rank XP saves an explicit snapshot in per-workspace app preferences. Start → Apply pending PAK edits writes only that snapshot to the workspace, preserving the original; later preview edits are excluded until saved again. Staged XP survives restarts and is listed on Start even before the rank tab is opened. Apply staged rank XP before packing.
 
 All desktop tabs share one double-Shift text search with a three-character minimum. It searches the current tab and selected sub-tab, highlighting labels, values, table text and detail data without filtering rows. Enter focuses the first match; Esc, clicking elsewhere, or switching tabs/windows closes search.
 
-**Game data → Truck properties** lists truck names, classes, assigned tiers, fuel capacity, unlock rank, price, store countries, differential lock and verified obtainable regions/maps. Region information reuses Regions-Trucks, including randomized replacements and pending map changes; unavailable map data and unverified placements are not guessed. Click column headers to sort, or **Order by tier** for SS through FX followed by Unsorted. Hover a truck name to show its usual tile. Edit numeric cells or use the −/+ glyphs to adjust all explicitly defined values (10 L fuel, 1 rank, 1,000 price), bounded to the displayed ranges. Blank/inherited values stay unchanged. **Save preset / Load preset** exports/imports a versioned JSON snapshot; loading only previews matching workspace values. **Stage changes** persists an explicit snapshot across restarts and lists it on Start even before opening this tab. **Revert unstaged edits** restores that snapshot, **Revert staged changes** clears it, and **Reset to original values** previews the preserved baseline. Only Start → Apply pending PAK edits writes the updated workspace files, preserving unrelated XML and the original files; later unstaged edits are excluded. Reload properties discards unstaged edits. Staged values changed externally are rejected during Apply and can be reloaded and restaged.
